Conversation 2 Welcome to this week's of Book Talk.

42
00:03:48,780 --> 00:03:54,180
With me today is Heidi Brown, a historian who has written five critically acclaimed

43
00:03:54,180 --> 00:03:56,140
books about military history.

44
00:03:56,140 --> 00:03:57,900
Thanks for having me, John.

45
00:03:58,360 --> 00:04:03,340
I'm so excited to talk about my latest book, which was published last month.

46
00:04:03,780 --> 00:04:09,060
So, this book is a novel, your first attempt at that genre, and thus a bit of a

47
00:04:09,060 --> 00:04:09,820
departure for you.

48
00:04:10,100 --> 00:04:14,460
I'd say it's a major departure, as it's not just a work of fiction.

49
00:04:14,680 --> 00:04:17,560
It's set 200 years in the future.

50
00:04:17,560 --> 00:04:20,200
Right, so how did that happen?

51
00:04:20,620 --> 00:04:27,420
You spent three decades writing about the past and focusing on the 18th and 19th and

52
00:04:27,420 --> 00:04:29,660
now you're speculating about the future.

53
00:04:30,180 --> 00:04:35,740
Well, after years of researching soldiers and chronicling their lives during battle,

54
00:04:35,880 --> 00:04:41,160
I just started wondering about other facets of their lives, especially their

55
00:04:41,160 --> 00:04:43,780
personal lives. I can see that.

56
00:04:43,940 --> 00:04:49,220
Your novel is about soldiers, but it focuses on their relationships, especially the

57
00:04:49,220 --> 00:04:52,960
bonds between sons and mothers, and men and their wives.

58
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:58,940
Yes, that focus came about when I still intended to write another book of history.

59
00:04:59,440 --> 00:05:04,600
I started by researching soldiers' actual personal lives, studying their letters

60
00:05:04,600 --> 00:05:08,320
home. So, how did that history book become a novel?

61
00:05:08,320 --> 00:05:14,860
Well, I realised that the historical record was incomplete, so I'd either have to

62
00:05:14,860 --> 00:05:19,980
leave a of gaps or make a lot more assumptions than a historian should.

63
00:05:20,500 --> 00:05:25,120
But why write a novel set in the future, when your credentials are perfect for a

64
00:05:25,120 --> 00:05:31,340
historical novel? As a historian, any historical novel you write would have a lot of

65
00:05:31,340 --> 00:05:37,380
credibility. I felt too constrained working with the past, like what I wrote needed

66
00:05:37,380 --> 00:05:43,240
to be fact as opposed to But writing about the future gave me more freedom to

67
00:05:43,240 --> 00:05:44,840
imagine, to invent.

68
00:05:45,420 --> 00:05:50,560
Well, having read your book, I'm glad you made that choice to move into fiction.

