83
00:07:47,680 --> 00:07:53,280
Most Americans don't drink soda out of the glass bottles seen in Coke's ads anymore.

84
00:07:53,740 --> 00:07:58,840
But this week, the company is celebrating a century of the bottle that's been sold

85
00:07:58,840 --> 00:08:00,980
in more than 200 countries.

86
00:08:00,980 --> 00:08:07,420
Flashback to 1915, when a bottle of Coca -Cola cost just a nickel.

87
00:08:07,840 --> 00:08:13,380
As the soft drink gained in popularity, it faced a growing number of competitors,

88
00:08:13,980 --> 00:08:17,100
counterfeits even trying to copy Coke's logo.

89
00:08:17,640 --> 00:08:23,300
So according to Coca -Cola historian Ted Ryan, company decided to come up with

90
00:08:23,300 --> 00:08:25,440
packaging that couldn't be duplicated.

91
00:08:26,020 --> 00:08:29,680
A product request was sent to eight different glassmakers.

92
00:08:29,680 --> 00:08:34,980
Workers at the Root Glass Company got the request and began flipping through the

93
00:08:34,980 --> 00:08:39,340
encyclopedia at the local library, landing on cocoa seed.

94
00:08:39,340 --> 00:08:45,340
Though cocoa seed is not an ingredient of the soda, they designed their bottle based

95
00:08:45,340 --> 00:08:47,960
on the seed's shape and large middle.

96
00:08:48,380 --> 00:08:54,100
It won over Coke executives in Atlanta and would go on to receive its own trademark.

97
00:08:54,840 --> 00:09:00,720
Spur collections and earn Coca -Cola an iconic image that made it part of American

98
00:09:00,720 --> 00:09:02,300
culture for a century.

99
00:09:02,300 --> 00:09:06,680
It was 100 years ago this week that the bottle earned a patent.

100
00:09:07,240 --> 00:09:11,700
By World War II, Coke bottle sales had ballooned into billions.

101
00:09:12,360 --> 00:09:17,760
Americans mostly consume Coke out of aluminum or plastic today, but the glass bottle

102
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:22,760
