Passage 2. Research shows that a few moments of conversation with a stranger creates

109
00:10:31,440 --> 00:10:33,360
a measurable improvement in mood.

110
00:10:33,360 --> 00:10:38,400
But most of us are reluctant to start these conversations because we presume the

111
00:10:38,400 --> 00:10:44,640
opposite. an experiment, commuters who talked to nearby strangers found their

112
00:10:44,640 --> 00:10:47,240
commute more enjoyable than those who didn't.

113
00:10:47,920 --> 00:10:52,220
They were asked to whether they'd enjoy the commute more if they conversed with

114
00:10:52,220 --> 00:10:57,880
other people. Intriguingly, most expected the more solitary experience to be more

115
00:10:57,880 --> 00:10:59,800
pleasurable. Why is this?

116
00:10:59,800 --> 00:11:03,800
Social anxiety appears to be problem.

117
00:11:04,480 --> 00:11:09,240
People's reluctance to start conversations with nearby strangers comes partly from

118
00:11:09,240 --> 00:11:12,240
underestimating others' interest in connecting.

119
00:11:12,940 --> 00:11:18,240
The sad thing is that people presume that a nearby stranger doesn't want to converse

120
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:20,090
and don't start a conversation.

121
00:11:20,940 --> 00:11:25,620
Only those who forced themselves to chat because it was required by the experiment

122
00:11:25,620 --> 00:11:28,620
found out what a pleasant experience it could be.

123
00:11:28,620 --> 00:11:31,340
Human beings are social animals.

124
00:11:31,980 --> 00:11:37,220
Those who misunderstand the impact of social interactions may not, in some contexts,

125
00:11:37,420 --> 00:11:39,320
be social enough for their own well -being.

126
00:11:40,180 --> 00:11:42,820
You should be chatting with the strangers you encounter.

127
00:11:43,400 --> 00:11:47,020
You may occasionally have a negative encounter that might stick in your memory.

128
00:11:47,460 --> 00:11:51,740
This is because the human brain is biased to dwell on negative events.

129
00:11:52,140 --> 00:11:57,260
But starting conversations with strangers is still well worth the risk of rejection.

130
00:11:57,260 --> 00:12:02,940
It may surprise you that conversing with strangers will make them happier too.

131
00:12:03,520 --> 00:12:06,120
The pleasure of connection seems contagious.

132
00:12:06,960 --> 00:12:12,520
People who are talked to have equally positive experiences as those who initiate a

