00:14:03,620 --> 00:14:09,180
The Caribbean islands are divided into two worlds, a rich one and a poor one.

146
00:14:09,180 --> 00:14:14,040
This tropical region's economy is based mainly on farming.

147
00:14:14,620 --> 00:14:16,060
Farmers are of two types.

148
00:14:16,560 --> 00:14:21,060
One is the plantation owner, who may have hundreds of thousands of acres.

149
00:14:21,620 --> 00:14:27,120
In contrast, the small cultivator is working only a few acres of land.

150
00:14:27,680 --> 00:14:30,500
Most visitors to the Caribbean are rich.

151
00:14:30,500 --> 00:14:36,900
Like the plantation owner, they do not realize, or do not want to realize, that many

152
00:14:36,900 --> 00:14:40,880
farm families barely manage to get by on what they grow.

153
00:14:41,640 --> 00:14:44,240
The Caribbean produces many things.

154
00:14:44,400 --> 00:14:46,140
Sugar is the main product.

155
00:14:46,500 --> 00:14:53,480
Other export crops are tobacco, coffee, bananas, spices and citrus fruits, such as

156
00:14:53,480 --> 00:14:55,300
orange, lemon or grapefruit.

157
00:14:55,300 --> 00:15:01,640
From the West Indies also come oil, mineral pitch and many forest products.

158
00:15:01,960 --> 00:15:05,320
Jamaica's aluminum ore supplies are the world's largest.

159
00:15:05,740 --> 00:15:08,740
Oil comes from Trinidad, Aruba and Caracas.

160
00:15:09,540 --> 00:15:13,660
But for many of the smaller islands, sugar is the only export.

161
00:15:14,440 --> 00:15:20,100
Rum, a strong alcoholic drink, which is distilled from sugar cane, is also an

162
00:15:20,100 --> 00:15:23,600
export. The world's best rum comes from this area.

163
00:15:23,600 --> 00:15:30,020
Local kinds vary, from the light rums of Puerto Rico to the heavier darker rums of

164
00:15:30,020 --> 00:15:31,540
Barbados and Jamaica.

165
00:15:32,160 --> 00:15:37,980
American tourists enjoy stocking up on inexpensive, high -quality Caribbean rum

166
00:15:37,980 --> 00:15:39,720
while they are on vacation.

167
00:15:40,380 --> 00:15:46,680
In Caracas, the well -known liquor of that name is made from the thick outer skin of

168
00:15:46,680 --> 00:15:47,760
a native orange.

169
00:15:47,760 --> 00:15:53,760
Ever since America's colonial days, the Caribbean islands have been favorite places

170
00:15:53,760 --> 00:15:58,280
to visit. Since World War II, tourism has increased rapidly.

171
00:15:58,780 --> 00:16:03,440
Because great numbers of people go there, the islanders have built elaborate

172
00:16:03,440 --> 00:16:10,220
resorts, developed harbors and airfields, improved beaches and have expanded sea and

173
00:16:10,220 --> 00:16:13,660
air routes. Everything is at the resort.

174
00:16:14,040 --> 00:16:17,180
Hotel, beach, shopping and recreation.

175
00:16:17,800 --> 00:16:21,340
The vacationer never has any reason to explore the island.

176
00:16:22,240 --> 00:16:26,800
As in most places, those who have money live well indeed.

177
00:16:27,280 --> 00:16:31,160
Those who don't have money live at various levels of poverty.

178
00:16:31,600 --> 00:16:34,860
But here, the poor greatly outnumber the wealthy.

179
00:16:34,860 --> 00:16:40,740
A visitor will find rich people living in apartments or Spanish houses at the

180
00:16:40,740 --> 00:16:42,820
seaside or in the countryside.

181
00:16:43,360 --> 00:16:47,900
Their servants might include a cook, a maid and a nurse for the children.

182
00:16:48,800 --> 00:16:51,520
Most of the people live well below the poverty level.

183
00:16:52,080 --> 00:16:55,110
In towns they live crowded together in tiny houses.

184
00:16:55,960 --> 00:16:59,080
Islanders make the best they can of what they have.

185
00:16:59,380 --> 00:17:01,000
Their homes are quite shabby.

186
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:05,640
Sadly, most tourists never see this side of the Caribbean.

