Recording 2. Talk to anyone who a generation or two older and they would most likely

191
00:18:13,980 --> 00:18:17,020
comment that children are more spoiled these days.

192
00:18:17,580 --> 00:18:22,680
No one wants to have or be around demanding, selfish and spoiled children.

193
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:27,800
Those who get bad tempered or silently brood when they're not given everything they

194
00:18:27,800 --> 00:18:33,540
want immediately. Paradoxically, the parents of such children encourage this

195
00:18:33,540 --> 00:18:38,400
demanding behaviour in the mistaken belief that by giving their children everything

196
00:18:38,400 --> 00:18:40,500
they can, their children will be happy.

197
00:18:41,120 --> 00:18:43,640
In the short term, perhaps they are right.

198
00:18:44,080 --> 00:18:49,340
But in the longer term, such children end up lonely, dependent, chronically

199
00:18:49,340 --> 00:18:54,480
dissatisfied and resentful of the parents who tried so hard to please them.

200
00:18:54,480 --> 00:19:00,740
Undoubtedly, parents want to happy children who are confident, capable and likeable

201
00:19:00,740 --> 00:19:02,400
rather than spoiled and miserable.

202
00:19:02,940 --> 00:19:08,860
One factor hindering this is that parents can't or don't spend enough quality time

203
00:19:08,860 --> 00:19:15,300
with their kids and substitute this deficit with toys, games, gadgets and the like.

204
00:19:15,400 --> 00:19:20,260
Rather than getting material things, children need parents to vote to detention.

205
00:19:20,260 --> 00:19:26,580
The quantity of time spent together is less important than the content of that time.

206
00:19:27,020 --> 00:19:32,000
Instead of instantly satisfying their wishes, parents should help them work out a

207
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:34,380
plan to earn things they'd like to have.

208
00:19:34,860 --> 00:19:39,260
This teaches them to value their effort as well as what it achieves.

209
00:19:39,260 --> 00:19:42,520
Allow them to anticipation.

210
00:19:43,020 --> 00:19:47,020
Numerous psychological studies have demonstrated that children who learn to wait for

211
00:19:47,020 --> 00:19:52,020
things they desire are more likely to succeed in a number of ways later in life.

212
00:19:52,520 --> 00:19:58,260
One famous experiment in the 1960s involved three to six -year -old children.

213
00:19:58,800 --> 00:20:03,300
They were given a choice between receiving a small reward, such as a cookie,

214
00:20:03,800 --> 00:20:07,560
immediately, or if they waited 15 minutes, they could have two.

215
00:20:07,560 --> 00:20:13,520
Follow -up studies have found that those who chose to delay satisfaction are now

216
00:20:13,520 --> 00:20:18,380
more academically successful, have greater self -worth and even tend to be

217
00:20:18,380 --> 00:20:24,300
healthier. If they fail, children should be encouraged to keep trying rather than to

218
00:20:24,300 --> 00:20:27,160
give up if they really want the desired result.

219
00:20:27,160 --> 00:20:31,920
This teaches them how to handle and recover from disappointment,

220
00:20:32,600 --> 00:20:38,520
is associated with greater success and satisfaction academically, financially and in

221
00:20:38,520 --> 00:20:43,780
personal relationships. And lastly, parents should encourage their children to look

222
00:20:43,780 --> 00:20:46,980
at life from other points of view as well as their own.

223
00:20:47,420 --> 00:20:53,060
This teaches them to be understanding of and sympathetic towards others, qualities

224
00:20:53,060 --> 00:20:55,780
sure to take them a long way in life.

