234
00:22:25,340 --> 00:22:28,260
The most obvious thing not to do is complain.

235
00:22:28,260 --> 00:22:31,020
Employers want to hire positive people.

236
00:22:31,640 --> 00:22:36,800
Talking about a previous job negatively raises concerns that you might be difficult

237
00:22:36,800 --> 00:22:41,900
to manage, or you might be someone that blames management for your own poor

238
00:22:41,900 --> 00:22:46,940
performance. Don't say that you've moved around in jobs because you haven't found

239
00:22:46,940 --> 00:22:50,300
the right fit or feel that you were not challenged enough.

240
00:22:50,960 --> 00:22:54,720
Statements like these will make you sound aimless and lost.

241
00:22:54,720 --> 00:22:59,640
An interviewer may well think, why would this role be any different for you?

242
00:23:00,220 --> 00:23:02,740
You will probably leave here in six months.

243
00:23:03,300 --> 00:23:07,600
It also begs the question of what type of relationship you had with your manager.

244
00:23:08,400 --> 00:23:12,800
It doesn't sound like you had open communication with him or her.

245
00:23:13,260 --> 00:23:18,400
Managers usually love people who can self sustain and enable growth through taking

246
00:23:18,400 --> 00:23:23,860
initiative. Who are strong at following through their work and who bring ideas and

247
00:23:23,860 --> 00:23:25,080
solutions to the table.

248
00:23:26,200 --> 00:23:30,320
If you were in a management or leadership position, when discussing your current

249
00:23:30,320 --> 00:23:34,460
role, never take all the credit for accomplishments or achievements.

250
00:23:35,100 --> 00:23:39,820
Emphasize your team and how, through their talents, your vision was realized.

251
00:23:40,420 --> 00:23:44,380
Most successful leaders know that they are only as good as their team.

252
00:23:44,380 --> 00:23:50,020
And acknowledging this in an interview will go a long way towards suggesting that

253
00:23:50,020 --> 00:23:54,380
you might be the right person for the position you are applying for.

254
00:23:55,060 --> 00:24:01,420
Lastly, have a good idea of what your role will be and try and convey the idea that

255
00:24:01,420 --> 00:24:06,720
you're flexible. Asking what your role will be suggests you will limit yourself

256
00:24:06,720 --> 00:24:08,700
purely to what is expected of you.

257
00:24:09,140 --> 00:24:12,480
In reality, your role is whatever you make of it.

258
00:24:12,480 --> 00:24:18,160
This is especially true in small companies where the ability to adapt and take on

259
00:24:18,160 --> 00:24:20,860
new responsibilities is highly valued.

260
00:24:21,500 --> 00:24:25,320
And this is equally important if you're just starting out.

261
00:24:25,680 --> 00:24:31,380
Entry level interviewees would do well to demonstrate a broad set of in most

262
00:24:31,380 --> 00:24:35,460
interviews. It's important to have a wide skill set.

263
00:24:35,460 --> 00:24:40,860
As many start -ups and small companies are moving really fast, employers are looking

264
00:24:40,860 --> 00:24:46,300
for candidates that are intelligent and can quickly adapt and excel in a growing

265
